+# Backend exception and recovery repairs — 2026-10-05
+
+Owner request: fix all P1/P2 findings in [the exception review](BACKEND_EXCEPTION_REVIEW_2026_10_05.md), with appropriate tests. Requirements B01–B07, B19–B20, B23, WR03–WR08, RW05–RW07 and Q01. Production remains a future cloud deployment with load-balanced APIs and independently scaled compatible workers. This task changes source/tests only: existing services, real player data, cloud resources and deployment are untouched.
+
+## Finding-to-repair mapping
+
+| Finding | Resulting behavior |
+| --- | --- |
+| 1 / P1 save lifetime | A global completed-result service owns recordings independently of game/menu nodes. Failed writes remain recoverable through Uploads → Retry saving. Inputs remain intact when the completed game clears/frees its array. Saves are tracked per attempt. Memory is bounded to 16 recordings/432,000 input frames; verified-start admission reserves space for a maximum recording. Ordinary offline racing remains available. |
+| 2 / P1 mixed API transport | Definitive unsupported compression/packed-envelope replies retry canonical legacy transport with the exact same ticket, operation key, controls, launch marker and receipts. A fleet-wide `BMT_TRANSPORT_PROFILE=legacy` capability floor is available while old API targets drain; switch to compact after compatibility acceptance. Modern refresh/resume request markers are strict body fields, so an old schema rejects them before mutation rather than silently executing an unrecoverable legacy charge/rotation. |
+| 3 / P1 wrong worker | Indexed queue selection joins the pinned Board and filters actual engine/rules/physics/compiler/schema/tick/laps/vehicle/handling/config before claim. An incapable worker spends no attempt. Verification keeps immutable geometry/hash and the exact claimed cohort's actual build. Absent compatible capacity for the configured two-hour wait releases admission as retryable `build_unavailable`, retaining original evidence; a matching live heartbeat prevents this timeout. Retry also checks the original vehicle/config. |
+| 4 / P2 malformed success | Endpoint-specific success validation turns missing/wrong fields into bounded protocol failures before state/cache changes. The outbox also validates batch/run data defensively and releases its flush latch. A corrected response can recover the same saved recording without restarting the app. Browser handoff, credentials, resources, tickets, runs, creator heads/publication and rivalry result shapes are distinguished. |
+| 5 / P2 refresh failure | Modern refresh persists a private 192-bit operation identifier before delivery. A bounded same-operation retry reproduces one replacement without storing plaintext credentials in the DB. Unknown delivery can recover across API/client restart without signing out. Different-operation or legacy consumed-token reuse still revokes the family; expiry/revocation/disabled-account checks remain. |
+| 6 / P2 uncertain resume | A small journal is written before beginning/consuming and records delivery before applying the rewind. Active pending selection stays paused. After leaving/restart, recovery inspects/confirms/abandons; it never replays a charge for an abandoned race. Server abandonment permanently closes an unsubmitted attempt before returning the requested unsettled resource once. Submitted attempts cannot refund. |
+| 7 / P2 missing Run | A missing pending status resubmits original retained ticket/key/content, recovering a consistent pre-submission restore point. Repeated dangling retry responses become an explicit support-recovery outcome. Expired/invalid cases stop rather than polling forever; proof files remain preserved until explicit dismissal. |
+| 8 / P2 outage/restart | Existing recently added signal-draining/readiness repairs are preserved. A surviving worker retains its computed bounded timing/manifest proof during failed SQL finalization and retries the original fence before claiming new work, avoiding another simulation/lease wait. Hard-kill uses existing lease expiry. Failed infrastructure Runs receive bounded automatic client recovery with persisted retry identity; definitive incompatibility remains explicit. |
+| 9 / P2 public budget spoof | A supplied header no longer grants an elevated budget. Only a DB-validated identity gets the larger NAT edge budget and its own authoritative weighted player budget. Mutations revalidate after body delivery. Fake credentials remain subject to anonymous limits and cannot access protected data. |
+| 10 / P2 clock | Server-time samples anchor new timestamped keys and advance monotonically. If no trusted sample exists, a cryptographic legacy opaque key is used instead of guessing a phone timestamp. Existing keys are preserved. Outbox waits use monotonic deadlines with bounded persisted restart delays; phone clock changes do not strand or accelerate pending operations. |
+| 11 / P2 error taxonomy | Only canonical `VerificationError` means invalid recording/construction. Storage/metadata/adapter ValueErrors are infrastructure failures with retained retryable evidence. Tests use the explicit canonical exception for genuine rejection. |
+| 12 / P2 observability | Existing worker duration/lifecycle logging and bounded readiness repairs are retained. Competition health now exposes worker service-time samples alongside compatible capacity, queue age and recovery metrics. Outage retries use bounded backoff/jitter; rivalry keeps infrastructure failure pending while recovery continues. Production account messages describe reconnect/sign-in/local play rather than PC setup. |
+
+## Authority and recovery policies
+
+Schema `0015_exception_recovery` adds nullable refresh operation hashes/nonces/replacement/time and server-owned resume abandoned/settled/refunded state. Back up and migrate before matching API/worker/client rollout. No existing installation was migrated. Downgrade must use a matching backup rather than discarding refund/recovery state.
+
+Refresh recovery is a narrow application protocol: both the previous refresh secret and the independent private operation secret are required within 120 seconds (configuration maximum 300), with a live, unconsumed replacement in the same session family. Server credentials are derived with domain-separated HMAC-SHA256 and a fresh server nonce; only hashes/nonces are stored. Family-first locking plus conditional token consumption preserves one replacement across PostgreSQL and SQLite concurrent retries. A different operation still detects reuse and revokes replacements. Legacy requests keep strict rotation.
+
+This is not DPoP or a claim of protection against theft of the complete private credential/operation pair. TLS, private application storage, no credential logging, short recovery windows and ordinary reauthentication remain necessary. The security tradeoff is explicit and tested; [RFC 9700 refresh protection](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9700.html#section-4.14) explains why rotation/reuse detection must remain.
+
+Resume recovery returns a banked credit only for the requested unsettled spend after the whole unsubmitted attempt becomes permanently ineligible for online submission. It restores the same-day free allowance only within its UTC day; expired daily resources never roll over, and temporary ad_preview receipts never mint banked rewards. Confirmation records a delivered spend; a confirmed receipt is not refunded. Player→ticket→race locking makes submission and abandonment mutually exclusive. The original timeline/three-resume/exact-receipt rules remain.
+
+Modern unresolved recovery evidence is protected until resolution. Bounded retention batches close expired unsubmitted uncertainty older than the retention interval, return eligible banked resources and mark the receipt settled before pruning. This avoids permanent lost-device evidence growth. Legacy spends are already settled and retain their earlier semantics. Production ad/purchase fulfillment remains unconfigured.
+
+Completed recordings cannot be persisted to a full/unwritable device. While the app stays alive, the new service retains failed data and exposes recovery regardless of navigation. Hard process termination before any durable write can still lose that recording; in-progress race persistence was not added. The UI states that unsaved recovery requires keeping the app open. Memory reservation limits apply to verified attempts; the existing offline race choice preserves unlimited ordinary racing.
+
+Cloud compatibility must use a consistent capability floor or versioned routing and retain original-build workers for accepted cohorts. Transport fallback never changes physics/rules or score keys. Unsupported original cohorts retain explicit retry/support status; they are not silently rescored. API readiness, worker capability/progress and a verified synthetic/private workflow remain distinct operational checks.
+
